<title>USA: Toyota unit sets $100 mln CPI-linked debt.</title>
<headline>Toyota unit sets $100 mln CPI-linked debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of inflation-indexed securities from Toyota Motor Corp's Toyota Motor Credit Corp was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager J.P. Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>BORROWER TOYOTA MOTOR CREDIT CORP</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON CPI+3.2 PCT  MATURITY 2/15/2002</p>
<p>TYPE CPI-LINKED    ISS PRICE 100.00    FIRST PAY DATE 8/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S Aaa   YIELD CPI+3.2 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P AAA				   CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672</p>
</text>
